@EVGA the fan design trigger... hmm... some sort of allergy problem I forgot what it was called.
It just not good.
Although transparent shroud is nice.

 @vyor8837  2070 supports ray tracing, 2060 won't, it won't compete with the 2070 directly for this exact reason, theoretically not making the 2070 pointless at all. This much is confirmed (though they could always lie and try and cram RT into the 2060 but as it seems to be launching under the GTX series I don't see that happening without a massive 180 form nvidia)

If there's no ray tracing then they have to justify purchasing a 2060 through other means, increased efficiency etc..
If it was priced at £250 with the performance of a 1070 / 1070ti then I agree with Brother Ares, would make for a competitively priced card and good value in comparison to the rest of the existing 20 series. Somehow I don't see that happening, if I had to guess (and blindly admittedly) I'd say they're going to sell the 2060 at around £350 mark... just case.

@Brother Ares man, your numbers are all over the place. A quick check of Scan says the cheapest 1080 Ti is £650, so you were pretty close there. However, a more accepted average increase in performance from 1080 Ti to the 2080 Ti is more like 25%/30% (I've seen as low as 15% and as high as 40%). 

Then, you say 90% more cost for a 2080 Ti, when they can be had for £1100 (don't get me wrong, it's still outrageous pricing). Your own figures of £700+90% tells me you think they go for ~£1330.

My brief research suggests a fairer post would say something like 30% more performance for 80% more cost. Which is still ridiculous and I would expect the card to also cook me breakfast and give me blow jobs for that price. So nVidia can get stuffed. Just saying, your numbers seem a bit off.

@Brother Ares yep the 2080ti is at crap value and is a cash grab from Nvidia it's for those who have a lot of disposable income. 
The 2080 is pointless as the 1080ti outperforms it for 100$ less
The 2070 is marginally better than the 1080 for a marginally higher price and seems the most reasonable.
